<!-- SECTION 1: PURPOSE -->
<div class="content-section" style="margin-top:32px;">
  <div class="section-header">1. Purpose &amp; Scope of Training</div>
  <div class="content-body">
    <p>This training session was conducted to ensure that Virgilio Espericueta is properly qualified and authorized to operate a vertical mast aerial lift (Genie RunAbout) in accordance with OSHA 29 CFR 1926.453 and ANSI/SIA A92.2 standards. As a subcontractor finisher performing work at elevated heights, authorization to operate aerial lift equipment is a mandatory safety requirement on all YSD job sites.</p>
    <p>The session included both classroom-style instruction and hands-on practical evaluation on the actual equipment present on site — a Genie RunAbout (Unit #10658676, rented through United Rentals).</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: TOPICS -->
<div class="content-section">
  <div class="section-header">2. Training Topics Covered</div>
  <div class="content-body">
    <ul class="key-points">
      <li>Overview of OSHA 29 CFR 1926.453 aerial lift regulations and employer responsibilities</li>
      <li>Equipment familiarization: Genie RunAbout vertical mast lift components, controls, and rated platform capacity</li>
      <li>Pre-operation inspection checklist: hydraulic systems, platform railings, drive wheels, battery charge, and emergency lowering</li>
      <li>Safe operating procedures: positioning, ground conditions, overhead hazard clearance, and prohibited use cases</li>
      <li>Fall protection requirements while inside the platform: proper use of body harness and lanyard connection point</li>
      <li>Electrocution hazards: minimum approach distances to energized lines and equipment</li>
      <li>Emergency procedures: platform entrapment, manual lowering, and evacuation protocols</li>
      <li>Site-specific hazards recognition at the current job site</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

